      <problem>
        <paragraph>Suppose that $$F$$ , $$G$$ , and $$Q$$ are polynomials and</paragraph>
        <paragraph math="block">$$\frac{F(x)}{Q(x)} = \frac{G(x)}{Q(x)}$$</paragraph>
        <paragraph>for all $$x$$ except when $$Q(x) = 0$$ . Prove that $$F(x) = G(x)$$ for all $$x$$ . [Hint: Use continuity.]</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="76" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>Use integration by parts to show that, for any positive integer $$n$$ , $${\int\frac{dx}{{({x^{2} + a^{2}})}^{n}}}dx = \frac{x}{2a^{2}({n - 1}){({x^{2} + a^{2}})}^{n - 1}} + \frac{2n - 3}{2a^{2}({n - 1})}{\int\frac{dx}{{({x^{2} + a^{2}})}^{n - 1}}}$$</item>
          <item>Use part (a) to evaluate $$\int\frac{dx}{{({x^{2} + 1})}^{2}}$$ and $$\int\frac{dx}{{({x^{2} + 1})}^{3}}$$</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="77" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>If $$a \neq 0$$ and $$n$$ is a positive integer, find the partial fraction decomposition of $$f(x) = 1/{x^{n}({x - a})}$$ . [Hint: First find the coefficient of $$1/({x - a})$$ . Then subtract the resulting term and simplify what is left.]</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{1}{a^{n}({x - a})} - \frac{1}{a^{n}x} - \frac{1}{a^{n - 1}x^{2}} - \cdots - \frac{1}{ax^{n}}$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
